.TH UNLINKAT 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
unlinkat \- remove a directory-relative entry
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.BI "int unlinkat(int " directory ", const char* " path ", int " flags ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Resolves a relative path from the directory descriptor, or the current
directory for
.BR AT_FDCWD .
An absolute path ignores the descriptor.
With flags zero it removes a non-directory entry; with
.B AT_REMOVEDIR
it removes an empty directory.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero on success, leaving
.B errno
unchanged, or \-1 on failure with positive Linux
.BR errno .
.SH NOTES
Crunch errno is process\-wide.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unlink (3crunch),
.BR rmdir (3crunch),
.BR unlinkat (2)
